Why the LGPL does not reach this gem
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This gem is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and that remains
true, for a simpler reason than it would need if there were an extension here.

There is no extension here. Nothing in this gem compiles against, links, or is
derived from libshumate. What it contains is a twenty-line loader and the string
"Shumate". At runtime ruby-gnome's GObjectIntrospection::Loader reads the
typelib the installing machine already has and defines Ruby classes that call
into the library through libffi -- so the library is never shipped, never
bundled, and is always the recipient's own copy, which they can replace at will.

Section 6 of the LGPL also requires that this notice say the library is used and
where to get it, which the section above does.

The same holds for the libraries libshumate's typelib depends on, which the
loader resolves transitively from the same machine: GTK 4, GDK, GSK, Pango,
GdkPixbuf, HarfBuzz, Graphene and glib.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ruby-gnome
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The loader is modelled on ruby-gnome's own, which is how ruby-gnome ships
gtksourceview5, libsecret and the rest. `gobject-introspection` and `glib2`,
this gem's runtime dependencies beyond gem_kit, come from that project.

